{"kind":"stack","id":"stk-materials","title":"Changes that make new materials","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#073642","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Burning"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"When something burns, it reacts with oxygen and new materials form. Burning is usually not reversible."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"New material"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"A new material is a substance with different properties from the materials it was made from."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which of these is a change that makes a new material?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Burning paper","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Bending a ruler","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Melting ice into water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"What happens when vinegar, an acid, is mixed with bicarbonate of soda?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"A gas is produced and new materials form","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"The mixture gets colder and nothing else happens","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"The two substances simply mix and separate again","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Can you easily turn burnt toast back into bread?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"No, this change is not usually reversible","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Yes, by cooling it down","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"Yes, by adding water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"You find a box of old candles and a jar of bicarbonate of soda. What do you do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Light a candle and watch it burn","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Mix bicarbonate of soda with vinegar","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The candle burns. Wax melts, smoke rises, and the wick turns to ash. The change cannot easily be undone."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"The mixture fizzes and bubbles as a gas forms. New materials have been made, and the change is hard to reverse."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which sign shows that a new material has formed?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"A colour change or a gas bubbling out","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Something getting slightly bigger in size","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Something being moved to another place","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which change can usually be reversed?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Melting a chocolate bar and letting it set again","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Burning a piece of wood","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Baking a cake in the oven","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done: you explored changes that make new materials"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Keep looking for signs of change around you. Burning and acid reactions are not usually reversible."}],"actions":[]}}
